  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the sustainability of the shea supply chain in northern Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the aim to contribute to increased incomes and improved livelihoods among shea producing communities in the Northern region of Ghana, a consortium consisting of The Body Shop, Cargill ZOR, Tungtei, Solidaridad, The Lorna Young Foundation and Global Shea Alliance joined forces to contribute to a stronger and more resilient shea supply chain.The project empowered women shea producers in Northern Ghana by tackling gender inequality, economic marginalisation, health and safety issues, and environmental degradation. It focused on improving health, safety, and business management, and promoting income diversification. A combination of radio broadcasts and face-to-face training delivered culturally relevant information on shea parkland management, processing, cooperative development, and good agricultural practices, amplifying impact through partnerships.This initiative boosted women&apos;s economic status through business training, leading to better product quality, higher shea nut prices, and increased household incomes. It strengthened cooperatives, enhancing collective bargaining and social visibility, and empowered women through radio. The project also promoted sustainable shea parkland management and financial resilience training.As a result of this project more than 7,000 women have been reached directly on new practices related to health and safety (H&amp;S), business management, climate smart agriculture, crop diversification/vegetable production and sustainable shea parkland management. The ten nut collector associations have increased knowledge on health and safety practices and reporting, and have access to health and safety frameworks to continue the efforts on their own. The associations also have access to all recordings and materials from the radio station programmes, and have been equipped to facilitate their own radio shows or meetings to continue the efforts on sharing knowledge in the surrounding communities.</narrative>
  </description>
